This crate embeds tables compiled from the third-party sources below
(the generated files under src/, made from the snapshots in the data/
directory of https://github.com/public/ducat). Each section names the
source, its version and the date it was retrieved.

[ISO 4217 List One]
  ISO 4217 List One (current currency and funds code list), published
  by SIX Financial Information AG as the ISO 4217 maintenance agency,
  https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/financial-information/data-center/iso-currrency/lists/list-one.xml
  Snapshot published 2026-09-17, retrieved and checked against the live
  list 2026-11-07: the codes, names, numeric codes and minor units.
  ISO 4217 is a standard of the International Organization for
  Standardization.

[ISO 4217 List Three]
  ISO 4217 List Three (withdrawn currency and funds codes), published
  by SIX Financial Information AG as the ISO 4217 maintenance agency,
  https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/financial-information/data-center/iso-currrency/lists/list-three.xml
  Snapshot published 2026-01-01, retrieved 2026-11-08: the withdrawn
  codes, names, numeric codes and withdrawal dates.

[OpenJDK currency data]
  The minor units of withdrawn ISO 4217 codes, taken as facts from
  OpenJDK's CurrencyData.properties (dataVersion 180, GPLv2 with the
  Classpath Exception),
  https://github.com/openjdk/jdk/blob/master/src/java.base/share/data/currency/CurrencyData.properties
  retrieved 2026-11-08. List Three carries no minor units; none was
  verified against an ISO source directly.

[Unicode CLDR 49: currency data]
  Data from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR), release
  49: the <currencyData> of supplementalData.xml, the currencies each
  territory uses and used (with their dates and tender), and the cash
  digits and cash rounding of the currencies CLDR cash-rounds, from
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/unicode-org/cldr/release-49/common/supplemental/supplementalData.xml
  The snapshot records no retrieval date; it was taken on 2026-11-08,
  the day it was added to the repository.
  Used under the Unicode License v3 (SPDX: Unicode-3.0), whose text is
  in LICENSE-UNICODE. Copyright © Unicode, Inc.

[Cash-rounding rules]
  Cash rounding rules compiled from central-bank, statutory and
  government publications, retrieved 2026-11-07 (rules added later
  carry their own retrieval date). Each rule records its source URL and
  whether it was verified against a primary source.

[Crypto units]
  Decimals, names and contract addresses (facts) of crypto currencies
  and tokens, from the sources that define them, pinned to: Bitcoin
  Core v28.0 (src/consensus/amount.h), ethereum-lists/chains at commit
  e17474286275730fb6b0490b1d7ea1c64a36ed9e (eip155-1.json), the Solana
  SDK at commit dcc9f4df80afeaaa093316ab9d0dccba4ca55525
  (native-token), and the Uniswap default token list 22.34.0 for the
  Ethereum mainnet tokens. Retrieved 2026-11-08. Token names are their
  issuers'.

[Stripe documentation]
  Currency and minor-unit rules from Stripe's documentation,
  https://docs.stripe.com/currencies, retrieved 2026-11-07. Stripe is a
  trademark of Stripe, Inc.

[Adyen documentation]
  Currency codes and decimals from Adyen's documentation,
  https://docs.adyen.com/development-resources/currency-codes,
  retrieved 2026-11-07. Adyen is a trademark of Adyen N.V.

[Checkout.com documentation]
  Amount rules from Checkout.com's documentation,
  https://www.checkout.com/docs/payments/accept-payments/format-the-amount-value,
  https://www.checkout.com/docs/developer-resources/codes/currency-codes
  and https://api-reference.checkout.com/v1/swagger.json, retrieved
  2026-11-07. Checkout.com is a trademark of Checkout Ltd.

[PayPal documentation]
  Currency codes and decimals from PayPal's documentation,
  https://developer.paypal.com/api/rest/reference/currency-codes/,
  https://developer.paypal.com/reference/currency-codes/ and
  https://developer.paypal.com/api/orders/v2/schema.yaml, retrieved
  2026-11-07. PayPal is a trademark of PayPal, Inc.

[Braintree documentation]
  Supported currencies and zero-decimal currencies from Braintree's
  documentation,
  https://developer.paypal.com/braintree/docs/reference/general/currencies,
  https://developer.paypal.com/braintree/docs/reference/request/transaction/sale,
  https://developer.paypal.com/braintree/docs/reference/general/validation-errors/all/
  and https://developer.paypal.com/braintree/graphql/reference/types/amount,
  retrieved 2026-11-07. Braintree is a service of PayPal, Inc.

[Klarna documentation]
  Amount rules from Klarna's documentation,
  https://docs.klarna.com/acquirer/klarna/get-started/integration-resilience/data-types/,
  https://docs.klarna.com/klarna-payments/in-depth-knowledge/puchase-countries-currencies-locales/
  and https://docs.klarna.com/acquirer/klarna/api/payments/, retrieved
  2026-11-07. Klarna is a trademark of Klarna Bank AB.

The data is provided as is, with no warranty of accuracy. Check
processor rules against the processor's current documentation before
relying on them.
